<summary><strong>high</strong> timezone-dependent: yearLabel: yearLabel returns different results in different time zones</summary>

yearLabel takes no Date and no time zone argument, yet the same call returns a different value when the process runs with TZ=America/Sao_Paulo instead of TZ=UTC. Code like this usually mixes local time getters (getHours, getDate, getFullYear, toLocaleString) with UTC values, so results change near midnight and New Year, or between servers and browsers in different zones.

Expected: The same result in every time zone, or an explicit time zone parameter.

Minimal input: `0`

Confidence: medium, confirmed in a fresh process

Reproduction:

```js
// yearLabel returns different results in different time zones
// Found by breakhound. Package: buggy-lib@1.0.0
import { yearLabel } from 'buggy-lib';

for (const tz of ['UTC', 'America/Sao_Paulo']) {
  process.env.TZ = tz;
  console.log(tz, yearLabel(0));
}
```

Vitest test:

```ts
import { expect, test } from 'vitest';
import { yearLabel } from 'buggy-lib';

test("yearLabel does not depend on the host time zone", () => {
  const original = process.env.TZ;
  try {
    process.env.TZ = 'UTC';
    const expected = yearLabel(0);
    process.env.TZ = 'America/Sao_Paulo';
    expect(yearLabel(0)).toEqual(expected);
  } finally {
    if (original === undefined) delete process.env.TZ;
    else process.env.TZ = original;
  }
});
```

